WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.800
Did you know the entire plot of Malignant&nbsp;
is right there in the opening credits, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:06.320
you were too stupid to notice? Let’s start with&nbsp;
the credits themselves. Annabelle Wallis is the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:09.920
actress who plays the protag, Madison Mitchell.&nbsp;
All of the repeated letters in her name (that is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:14.080
the Ns, the Ls and the other Ls) start as one&nbsp;
letter, then divide into two. This process&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:17.760
mirrors the cell division that we later learn&nbsp;
occurred to create the parasitic twin, Gabriel.

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:20.720
The actual footage shown during the&nbsp;
title sequence also spoils the movie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:23.520
if you can comprehend it. It’s assumed&nbsp;
that the surgery clips we’re seeing are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:26.640
the procedure on Gabriel mentioned in the&nbsp;
opening, but stopping at just the right&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:30.720
moment shows that the patient name is Emily May;&nbsp;
which we later learn is Madison’s real name.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:33.360
A medical diagram shows a girl with&nbsp;
eyes looking in different directions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:37.280
as a result of the craniopagus, and Emily’s&nbsp;
file mentions sleepwalking, hallucinations,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:41.120
and waking dreams, all of which are eventually&nbsp;
attributed to Gabriel hijacking her brian.

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:45.760
– [Dr Weaver] We’re starting to suspect that Gabriel&nbsp;
can somehow access the regions of the brain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:50.240
that process visual stimuli and make&nbsp;
Emily see what she wants her to see.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:54.640
This would explain her recent claims&nbsp;
of hallucinations and waking dreams.

00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:58.000
– Another page adds malnourishment to&nbsp;
her list of symptoms. We come to find&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:01.360
out that Gabriel was essentially feeding&nbsp;
off of her fetuses to build himself back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:03.680
up. He was the hidden cause&nbsp;
of all of her miscarriages.

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:06.880
We even see brain scans that seem to highlight&nbsp;
the tumor on the backside of her head,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:10.800
and this file describes craniofacial&nbsp;
features including two fully formed faces,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:14.720
while making a comparison to Janus cats, a&nbsp;
rare condition in cats that causes them to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:18.720
be born with 2 faces. The name was inspired&nbsp;
by Janus, the Roman God of past and future,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:22.400
who is depicted as having two faces—one looking&nbsp;
into the past and one to the future.

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:23.600
Towards the end of the title sequence,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:27.120
a page in this binder spells out the&nbsp;
condition of craniopagus parasiticus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:31.040
which is the type of parasitic twinning that has&nbsp;
bound Madison and Gabriel to share one brain.

00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:34.800
There are many other clues about Malignant’s&nbsp;
terrifying twist nested throughout the entire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:37.520
movie, and many other Things You might&nbsp;
have Missed. To learn the meaning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:41.040
behind the hidden symbol on Detective Shaw’s&nbsp;
computer screen, the clue hidden in the movie’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:45.600
soundtrack and the meanings behind character names&nbsp;
and more, stick around to the end of this video.

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:47.978
