00:01:47.978 --> 00:01:54.240
(metal intro)

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:58.800
Welcome to Things You Missed. In 2016, director&nbsp;
James Wan released The Conjuring 2, his fourth&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:02.080
demonic possession movie. After this, he would&nbsp;
take a little break from the horror genre,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:05.840
but when he came back, he wanted to do something&nbsp;
new. He came back with an original concept,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.840 --> 00:02:10.400
developed by his wife, actress / writer-producer&nbsp;
Ingrid Bisu, who had a longtime fascination with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:14.800
teratomas and parasitic twins. Ingrid also has&nbsp;
a character in this movie named CST Winnie. I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:18.800
believe the CST stands for Crime Scene Technician.&nbsp;
She’s the one doing the hands-on investigating,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:22.160
and she’s clearly passionate about her job.&nbsp;
This would reflect her interest in the idea&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:26.800
of a villainous parasitic twin in real life. Her&nbsp;
character also has a crush on the asian detective.

00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:29.230
– [Det. Moss] Uh oh, here comes Ms. Lonelyheart.&nbsp;

00:02:29.230 --> 00:02:30.313
– Hey Kokoa.
– Winnie.

00:02:30.313 --> 00:02:33.840
– You have to believe this character represents&nbsp;
James Wan, the head of the investigation;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:37.680
the director of the movie. James wanted to get&nbsp;
back to his roots with a police procedural serial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:41.440
crime movie, like his breakout hit, Saw,&nbsp;
while also expanding into new territory.

00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:46.948
– [Wan] There’s a bit of mystery, there’s a&nbsp;
bit of creature feature monster aspect to it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.948 --> 00:02:48.958
there's a serial killer aspect.

00:02:48.958 --> 00:02:51.920
– He’s also talked about the influence&nbsp;
of Italian Giallo horror films like the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:56.080
nightmares of Dario Argento, and the body&nbsp;
horror stylings of David Cronenberg. I’ll&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.080 --> 00:02:59.200
get into some more specific examples&nbsp;
when we get into the Things You Missed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:01.769
so let’s get in to the Things You…

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:06.801
Why do we do&nbsp;
this? Why do we always open the show this way?

00:03:06.801 --> 00:03:12.480
(upbeat music)

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:15.920
The opening company logos are altered to&nbsp;
look like we’re watching them on an old CRT&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:19.360
monitor. This makes them match the video&nbsp;
diaries from the Simion Research Facility&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.360 --> 00:03:22.480
where we learn about Madison and Gabriel’s&nbsp;
past, but also might be a reference to what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:27.200
James Wan might have seen while watching old&nbsp;
Giallo films on TV as a teenager in the 1990s.

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:30.560
The first diary we see is from Emily&nbsp;
and Gabriel’s doctor, Florence Weaver,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:34.320
and she has a bust of a man with an exposed&nbsp;
brain. This is likely for demonstration purposes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:38.160
but it also serves as a precursor to Gabriel,&nbsp;
who emerges by poking through Madison’s skull.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:42.160
Also seen on the shelf is her Medical Research&nbsp;
Association Award, which later becomes Gabriel’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:46.400
main weapon. It is originally a large spike&nbsp;
surrounded by a tapering double snake helix and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:50.480
angelic wings. The helix, when viewed from above,&nbsp;
creates a spiral, a symbol that has become an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:54.640
element of James Wan’s auteur as a director.&nbsp;
I also noticed a similar tapering helix on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.640 --> 00:03:58.320
the plants outside Dr. Gregory’s apartment,&nbsp;
shortly before he’s taken out by Gabriel.

00:03:58.320 --> 00:04:02.000
Gabriel also makes his lair in the attic,&nbsp;
and we enter it via a big spiraling camera&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:05.760
movement as Gabriel makes modifications to&nbsp;
this trophy. This movement is also something&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:09.600
we’ve see before in Wan’s work, like this&nbsp;
shot in Saw, or this shot in Dead Silence.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:12.960
After removing the snakes, Gabriel keeps&nbsp;
the angelic wings, effectively serving as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:16.800
a hilt for his new weapon. This ties into a&nbsp;
theme that Madison talks about much later on,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:20.480
the idea that Gabriel is essentially a demon&nbsp;
in hiding. The name Gabriel comes from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:24.560
biblical messenger angel, Gabriel. I imagine&nbsp;
it was chosen to hide his true, evil nature.

00:04:26.071 --> 00:04:31.520
– [Emily] He pretends to be&nbsp;
nice. But he’s the devil.

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:35.280
– Gabriel likes to position himself in high&nbsp;
places. I already talked about the attic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:39.360
but he also attacks Serena from above, and he&nbsp;
attacks Shaw from above on multiple occasions.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:42.560
But when he’s discovered and chased,&nbsp;
he retreats to where he’s most at home,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.560 --> 00:04:46.160
the Seattle Underground; representative&nbsp;
of hell. It is also the basement of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.160 --> 00:04:49.520
research facility where Sydney discovers the&nbsp;
files containing the truth about Gabriel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.520 --> 00:04:52.080
where the graffiti makes the&nbsp;
analogy a little bit more obvious.

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:56.240
But the idea that Gabriel is a devil posing as&nbsp;
an angel is also reflected in the camera work.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.240 --> 00:04:59.840
Many of the attacks feature this top-down&nbsp;
view on the victim. The house even contains&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.840 --> 00:05:03.600
stained glass window artwork, something we’ve&nbsp;
certainly seen before in residential houses,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:05.920
but something you’re more likely&nbsp;
to associate with a church.

00:05:05.920 --> 00:05:08.880
The biblical Gabriel was a messenger&nbsp;
angel who communicated with the prophet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.880 --> 00:05:12.640
Daniel to explain his visions. Malignant’s&nbsp;
Gabriel literally gives Madison visions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.640 --> 00:05:14.880
and communicates with her via TVs and radios.

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:18.800
Gabriel’s mother, Serena, might have predicted his&nbsp;
true nature if she had listened to her parents.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.800 --> 00:05:22.480
In one of the tapes she explains her Mom and&nbsp;
Dad were religious, and saw the teen pregnancy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.480 --> 00:05:26.480
as a transgression against God. Finally, the&nbsp;
police gather information on Serena and if you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.480 --> 00:05:30.800
look carefully, her Social Security Number&nbsp;
begins with 666, the number of the devil.

00:05:30.800 --> 00:05:33.760
After the intro with Dr. Weaver,&nbsp;
we meet the current day Emily May,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.760 --> 00:05:36.640
who now goes by Madison Mitchell. She&nbsp;
has a child of her own on the way,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:40.160
but when Gabriel comes back into her&nbsp;
life, we can spot even more secrets.

